From bbdf65dedf4ac244a55c42fefad12edeb50e7270 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michiel <367462+meghuizen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:34:00 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH net-next 3/4] net: gro: find the offload before preparing
 the gro list

dev_gro_receive() calls gro_list_prepare() before it looks up the
packet_offload for skb->protocol.  gro_list_prepare() compares the skb
with every skb held in its bucket, up to MAX_GRO_SKBS, and sets
NAPI_GRO_CB(p)->same_flow on each.  When the protocol has no
->gro_receive (ARP, PPPoE session frames), the skb goes to 'normal' and
those results are never read.

Call gro_list_prepare() once the offload has been found.  same_flow on
the held skbs is read only by the ->gro_receive callbacks, and the next
gro_list_prepare() rewrites it.  For protocols with an offload the work
is the same, in a different order.

Not measured.  The saving is one walk of the bucket's held skbs per
packet without an offload, and nothing when the bucket is empty.

Tested: gro.o builds without warnings (W=1) on x86_64.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
Impact: low -- GRO receive of protocols without a GRO offload (ARP,
PPPoE session) while the bucket holds packets.  Not measured.

 net/core/gro.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/core/gro.c b/net/core/gro.c
index 29b4d02bf519..6dbb7adf77d0 100644
--- a/net/core/gro.c
+++ b/net/core/gro.c
@@ -488,8 +488,6 @@ static enum gro_result dev_gro_receive(struct gro_node *gro,
 	if (netif_elide_gro(skb->dev))
 		goto normal;
 
-	gro_list_prepare(&gro_list->list, skb);
-
 	rcu_read_lock();
 	list_for_each_entry_rcu(ptype, head, list) {
 		if (ptype->type == type && ptype->callbacks.gro_receive)
@@ -499,6 +497,8 @@ static enum gro_result dev_gro_receive(struct gro_node *gro,
 	goto normal;
 
 found_ptype:
+	gro_list_prepare(&gro_list->list, skb);
+
 	skb_set_network_header(skb, skb_gro_offset(skb));
 	skb_reset_mac_len(skb);
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(sizeof_field(struct napi_gro_cb, zeroed) != sizeof(u32));
-- 
